VIOLATION — compliant=false, with four breaches named, all four inside the two numbered clauses.

First, clause 1's HEADING states an obligation while its BODY hedges throughout — should
generally, are encouraged to move toward, where that seems proportionate, usually less safe,
tends to be worth avoiding, may reasonably be retained — and its closing sentence hands back the
very case the heading forbids: leaving the normalize in the comparison and the stored value as
it arrived is called "an acceptable steady state". The clause forbids comparison-time
normalization in its title and permits it in its last line.

Second, clause 1's `**BLOCKED rationalizations:**` heading is present and holds six ABSTRACT
CATEGORY LABELS instead of the literal first-person sentences a session emits —
premature-optimization reasoning, single-consumer assumptions, delegation to a lower layer,
client-behaviour extrapolation, read-path compensation, deferred-remediation planning. No
session ever writes those words, so the corpus traps nothing. Clause 2's corpus is the real
thing and is byte-identical with the sibling pole, which is the point: the defect is local to
clause 1's corpus, not to the presence of a corpus.

Third, clause 2's worked block has two arms that are the SAME LINE — the identical
`unicodedata.normalize("NFC", row.handle)` assignment — separated only by the adverbs promptly
and belatedly. The contrast slot is filled and carries no contrast, and worse, the DO arm
teaches the repairing read that the clause's own prose names BLOCKED two lines above it.

Fourth, clause 2's `**Why:**` runs well past the two-sentence cap, wandering into the database
collation, the client population's skew, the share of traffic reaching the repairing reader,
whether the column is indexed, whether a periodic backfill already runs, and how quickly the bad
writer could be found by other means. The justification ends up arguing that the obligation's
importance is conditional on six things.

Surface-equalized with the sibling pole: identical frontmatter, identical title and preamble,
identical `## ` heading skeleton, two numbered clauses each, one worked block per clause each,
one `**BLOCKED rationalizations:**` heading per clause each.

The frontmatter, the whole `## MUST NOT` section including its one-sentence justification, the
entire `## Trust Posture Wiring` block with its eight canonical fields and its
structurally-grounded Phase-2 deferral, and the whole `## Origin` section are shared
byte-for-byte and are NOT findings. Clause 2's heading, its normative sentence, its BLOCKED
corpus and clause 1's `**Why:**` are shared too. A judge naming any of them — or naming the
deferred detector, the fictional rule, the priority, or the file length — has scored furniture
rather than content.
